            = succeed "-formulation" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/jet+bundle"} jet bundle
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/variational+calculus"} variational calculus
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+field+theory"} Lagrangian field theory
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a{:href => "#FieldVariations"} 4. Field variations
            %em
              %a{:href => "#Lagrangians"} 5. Lagrangians
            we follow
            %a{:href => "variational+bicomplex#Anderson89"} Anderson 89
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Olver86"} Olver 86
            = succeed ";" do
              %a{:href => "smooth+set#GiotopoulosSati23"} Giotopoulos &amp; Sati 2023
            %em
              %a{:href => "#Symmetries"} 6. Symmetries
            augmented by
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#higher+prequantum+geometry#FRS13b"} Fiorenza-Rogers-Schreiber 13b
          %p
            The identification of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polynomial+observables"} polynomial observables
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distributions"} distributions
            in
            %em
              %a{:href => "#Observables"} 7. Observables
            was observed by
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "distributions+are+the+smooth+linear+functionals#Paugam12"} Paugam 12
          %p
            The discussion of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peierls-Poisson+bracket"} Peierls-Poisson bracket
            in
            %em
              %a{:href => "#PhaseSpace"} 8. Phase space
            is based on
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "Peierls+bracket#Khavkine14"} Khavkine 14
          %p
            The derivation of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wave+front+sets"} wave front sets
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propagators"} propagators
            in
            %em
              %a{:href => "#Propagators"} 9. Propagators
            takes clues from
            %a{:href => "Hadamard+distribution#Radzikowski96"} Radzikowski 96
            and uses results from
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "Cauchy+principal+value#GelfandShilov66"} Gelfand-Shilov 66
          %p
            For the general idea of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BV-BRST+formalism"} BV-BRST formalism
            a good review is
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "BV-BRST+formalism#Henneaux90"} Henneaux 90
          %p
            The
            = succeed "-perspective" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebroid"} Lie algebroid
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BRST+complexes"} BRST complexes
            developed in chapter
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a{:href => "#GaugeSymmetries"} 10. Gauge symmetries
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "BRST+complex#Barnich10"} Barnich 10
          %p
