            %a{:href => "star+product#Collini16"} Collini 16
            and spells out the derivation of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Moyal+star+product"} Moyal star product
            from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+quantization+of+symplectic+groupoids"} geometric quantization of symplectic groupoids
            due to
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "Moyal+deformation+quantization#GBV"} Gracia-Bondia &amp; Varilly 94
          %p
            The perspective on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wick+algebra"} Wick algebra
            in
            %em
              %a{:href => "#FreeQuantumFields"} 14. Free quantum fields
            goes back to
            %a{:href => "Wick+algebra#Dito90"} Dito 90
            and was revived for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pAQFT"} pAQFT
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "Wick+algebra#DuetschFredenhagen00"} Dütsch-Fredenhagen 00
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hadamard+vacuum+state"} Hadamard vacuum state
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wick+algebra"} Wick algebra
            is indeed a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/state+on+a+star-algebra"} state
            is cited from
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "Wick#algebra#Duetsch18"} Dütsch 18
          %p
            The discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/causal+perturbation+theory"} causal perturbation theory
            in
            %em
              %a{:href => "#InteractingQuantumFields"} 15. Interacting quantum fields
            follows the original
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "causal+perturbation+theory#EpsteinGlaser73"} Epstein-Glaser 73
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/star+product"} star product
            induced by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Feynman+propagator"} Feynman propagator
            was highlighted in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "perturbative+algebraic+quantum+field+theory#FredenhagenRejzner12"} Fredenhagen-Rejzner 12
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interacting+field+algebra+of+observables"} interacting field algebra of observables
            defined by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bogoliubov%27s+formula"} Bogoliubov's formula
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/causally+local+net"} causally local net
            in the sense of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Haag-Kastler+axioms"} Haag-Kastler axioms
            is that of
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "pAQFT#BrunettiFredenhagen00"} Brunetti-Fredenhagen 00
          %p
            Our derivation of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Feynman+diagrams"} Feynman diagrammatics
            follows
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "Feynman+diagram#Keller10"} Keller 10, chapter IV
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+master+equation"} quantum master equation
            follows
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "BV-BRST+formalism#Rejzner11"} Rejzner 11, section 5.1.3
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ward+identities"} Ward identities
            is informed by
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "Ward+identity#Duetsch18"} Dütsch 18, chapter 4
          %p
            In chapter
            %em
              %a{:href => "#Renormalization"} 16. Renormalization
            we take from
            %a{:href => "renormalization#BrunettiFredenhagen00"} Brunetti-Fredenhagen 00
            the perspective of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Epstein-Glaser+renormalization"} Epstein-Glaser renormalization
            via
