                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
            %p#SmoothFunctions
              %strong Abstract coordinate systems
            %p
              What characterizes
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+geometry"} differential geometry
              is that it models
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry"} geometry
              on
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuum"} continuum
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+line"} real line
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+products"} Cartesian products
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+structure"} smooth structure
              (def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CartesianSpacesAndSmoothFunctionsBetweenThem"}
              below). We may think of these
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+spaces"} Cartesian spaces
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
              as the “abstract
              = succeed "\u201D" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coordinate+systems"} coordinate systems
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+functions"} smooth functions
              between them as the “abstract
              = succeed "\u201D." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coordinate+transformations"} coordinate transformations
            %p
              We will eventually consider
              %a{:href => "#FieldBundles"} below
              much more general “
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+spaces"}> smooth spaces
              ”
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              than just the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+spaces"} Cartesian spaces
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon \mathbb{R}^n \to X
              mapping a Cartesian space smoothly into them. All structure on
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+smooth+spaces"} generalized smooth spaces
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is thereby reduced to
              %em compatible systems
              of structures on just
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+spaces"} Cartesian spaces
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon \mathbb{R}^n \to X
              = succeed "\u201D." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functorial+geometry"} functorial geometry
            %p
              Notice that the popular concept of a
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
              (def./prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SmoothManifoldInsideDiffeologicalSpaces"}
              below) is essentially that of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+space"} smooth space
              which
              %em locally looks just like
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon \mathbb{R}^n \to X
              which are (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+map"}> open
              )
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphisms"} isomorphisms
              onto their
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/images"} images
              %em fix
              such local coordinate identifications
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            %p
              In
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functorial+geometry"} functorial geometry
              we do not even focus attention on those
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon \mathbb{R}^n \to X
              that are isomorphisms onto their image, but consider
              %em all
              “probes” of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              by “abstract coordinate systems”. This makes
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+geometry"} differential geometry
              both simpler as well as more powerful. The analogous insight for
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+geometry"} algebraic geometry
              is due to
              = succeed ";" do
                %a{:href => "functorial+geometry#Grothendieck65"} Grothendieck 65
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+geometry"} differential geometry
              by
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "synthetic+differential+geometry#Lawvere67"} Lawvere 67
            %p
              This allows to combine the best of two superficially disjoint worlds: On the one hand we may reduce all constructions and computations to
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coordinates"} coordinates
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physics"} physics
              literature; on the other hand we have full conceptual control over the coordinate-free generalized spaces analyzed thereby. What makes this work is that all
              = succeed "-constructions" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coordinate"} coordinate
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functorial+geometry"} functorially
              considered over all abstract coordinate systems.
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
            #CartesianSpacesAndSmoothFunctionsBetweenThem.num_defn
              %h6#definition Definition
              %p
                %strong
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+spaces"} Cartesian spaces
                  and
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+functions"} smooth functions
                  between them)
              %p
                For
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
                we say that the set
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-tuples"} n-tuples
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
                is a
                = succeed "." do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian space
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coordinate+functions"} coordinate functions
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi x
                        %mi k
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      x^k \;\colon\; \mathbb{R}^n \longrightarrow \mathbb{R}
              %p
                which send an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-tuple"} n-tuple
                of real numbers to the
                = succeed "th" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo ∈
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo ,
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \in \{1, \cdots, n\}
              %p For
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                      %mo ⟶
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      f \;\colon\; \mathbb{R}^{n} \longrightarrow \mathbb{R}^{n'}
              %p
                any
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
                between
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+spaces"} Cartesian spaces
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partial+derivative"} partial derivative
                along the
                = succeed "th" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mfrac
                        %mrow
                          %mo ∂
                          %mi f
                        %mrow
                          %mo ∂
                          %msup
                            %mi x
                            %mi k
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                      %mo ⟶
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo ′
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\frac{\partial f}{\partial x^k}
                      \\;\colon\;
                      \\mathbb{R}^{n}
                      \\longrightarrow
                      \\mathbb{R}^{n'}
                      \\,.
              %p
                If this exists, we may in turn ask that the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partial+derivative"} partial derivative
                of the partial derivative exists
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mfrac
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mo ∂
                            %mn 2
                          %mi f
                        %mrow
                          %mo ∂
                          %msup
                            %mi x
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi k
                                %mn 1
                          %mo ∂
                          %msup
                            %mi x
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi k
                                %mn 2
                      %mo ≔
                      %mfrac
                        %mo ∂
                        %mrow
                          %mo ∂
                          %msup
                            %mi x
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi k
                                %mn 2
                      %mfrac
                        %mrow
                          %mo ∂
                          %mi f
                        %mrow
                          %mo ∂
                          %msup
                            %mi x
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi k
                                %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\frac{\partial^2 f}{\partial x^{k_1} \partial x^{k_2}}
                      \\coloneqq
                      \\frac{\partial}{\partial x^{k_2}} \frac{\partial f}{\partial x^{k_1}}
              %p and so on.
              %p
                A general higher
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partial+derivative"} partial derivative
                obtained this way is, if it exists, indexed by an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-tuple"} n-tuple
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers"} natural numbers
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi α
                      %mo ∈
                      %msup
                        %mi ℕ
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha \in \mathbb{N}^n
                and denoted
              #eq:PartialDerivativeWithManyIndices.maruku-equation
                %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo ∂
                        %mi α
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ≔
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mfrac
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mo ∂
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                              %mi α
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mi f
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mo ∂
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi α
                                %mn 1
                          %msup
                            %mi x
                            %mn 1
                          %msup
                            %mo ∂
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi α
                                %mn 2
                          %msup
                            %mi x
                            %mn 2
                          %mi ⋯
                          %msup
                            %mo ∂
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi α
                                %mi n
                          %msup
                            %mi x
                            %mi n
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ,
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\partial_\alpha
                      \\;\coloneqq\;
                      \\frac{
                      \\partial^{\vert \alpha \vert} f
                      }{
                      \\partial^{\alpha_1} x^1
                      \\partial^{\alpha_2} x^2
                      \\cdots
                      \\partial^{\alpha_n} x^n
                      }
                      \\,,
              %p
                where
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi α
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mo ≔
                      %munderover
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                        %mi n
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo =
                          %mn 1
                      %msub
                        %mi α
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\vert \alpha\vert} \coloneqq \underoverset{n}{i = 1}{\sum} \alpha_i
                is the total
                %em order
                of the partial derivative.
              %p
                If all partial derivative to all orders
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi α
                      %mo ∈
                      %msup
                        %mi ℕ
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha \in \mathbb{N}^n
                of a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                      %mo →
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon \mathbb{R}^n \to \mathbb{R}^{n'}
                exist, then
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                is called a
                = succeed "." do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+function"} smooth function
            %p
              Of course the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g \circ f
              of two smooth functions is again a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+function"} smooth function
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi ℝ
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi n
                                  %mn 2
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mi f
                            %mo ↗
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo ↘
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi g
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi ℝ
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi n
                                  %mn 1
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %mi g
                                %mo ∘
                                %mi f
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi ℝ
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi n
                                  %mn 3
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \&amp;&amp; \mathbb{R}^{n_2}
                    \\\
                    \&amp; {}^{\mathllap{f}}\nearrow &amp;&amp; \searrow^{\mathrlap{g}}
                    \\\
                    \\mathbb{R}^{n_1}
                    \&amp;&amp; \underset{g \circ f}{\longrightarrow} &amp;&amp;
                    \\mathbb{R}^{n_3}
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              The inclined reader may notice that this means that
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+spaces"} Cartesian spaces
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+functions"} smooth functions
              between them constitute a
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              (“
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CartSp"}> CartSp
              ”); but the reader not so inclined may ignore this.
            %p
              For the following it is useful to think of each
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian space
              as an
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  abstract
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coordinate+system"} coordinate system
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+smooth+spaces"} generalized smooth spaces
              (see the table
              = succeed ")," do
                %a{:href => "#NotionsOfGeometry"} below
            #CoordinateFunctionsAreSmoothFunctions.num_example
              %h6#example Example
              %p
                %strong
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coordinate+functions"} coordinate functions
                  are
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+functions"} smooth functions
              %p
                Given a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian space
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coordinate+functions"} coordinate functions
                (def.
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CartesianSpacesAndSmoothFunctionsBetweenThem"}
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi x
                        %mi k
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      x^k \;\colon\; \mathbb{R}^n \longrightarrow \mathbb{R}
              %p
                are
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+functions"} smooth functions
                (def.
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CartesianSpacesAndSmoothFunctionsBetweenThem"}
              %p For
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi n
                            %mn 1
                      %mo ⟶
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi n
                            %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      f \colon \mathbb{R}^{n_1} \longrightarrow \mathbb{R}^{n_2}
              %p
                any
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+function"} smooth function
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo ∈
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 2
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ⋯
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi n
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in \{1, 2, \cdots, n_2\}
                write
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mi a
                      %mo ≔
                      %msup
                        %mi x
                        %mi a
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi f
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi n
                            %mn 1
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi f
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi n
                            %mn 2
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi x
                            %mi a
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      f^a \coloneqq x^a \circ f
                      \\;\colon\;
                      \\mathbb{R}^{n_1}
                      \\overset{f}{\longrightarrow}
                      \\mathbb{R}^{n_2}
                      \\overset{x^a}{\longrightarrow}
                      \\mathbb{R}
              %p
                \. for its
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
                with this
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coordinate+function"} coordinate function
            #AlgebraOfSmoothFunctionsOnCartesianSpaces.num_example
              %h6#example_2 Example
              %p
                %strong
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+of+functions"} algebra of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+functions"} smooth functions
                  on
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+spaces"} Cartesian spaces
              %p
                For each
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℕ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ≔
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msub
                        %mi Hom
                        %mi CartSp
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^n)
                      \\;\coloneqq\;
                      Hom_{CartSp}(\mathbb{R}^n, \mathbb{R})
              %p
                of
                = succeed "-valued" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+number"} real number
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+functions"} smooth functions
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                      %mo →
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon \mathbb{R}^n \to \mathbb{R}
                on the
                = succeed "-dimensional" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian space
                (def.
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CartesianSpacesAndSmoothFunctionsBetweenThem"}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+algebra"} commutative
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+algebra"} associative algebra
                over the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
                by pointwise addition and multiplication in
                = succeed ":" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℝ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo ,
                      %mi g
                      %mo ∈
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f,g \in C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^n)
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in \mathbb{R}^n
              %ol
                %li
                  %p
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi f
                          %mo +
                          %mi g
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ≔
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo +
                          %mi g
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f + g)(x) \coloneqq f(x) + g(x)
                %li
                  %p
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi f
                          %mo ⋅
                          %mi g
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ≔
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ⋅
                          %mi g
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f \cdot g)(x) \coloneqq f(x) \cdot g(x)
                    \.
              %p The inclusion
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mover
                        %mo ↪
                        %mi const
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\mathbb{R} \overset{const}{\hookrightarrow} C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^n)
              %p
                is given by the
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constant+functions"} constant functions
              %p
                We call this the
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+of+functions"} algebra of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+functions"} smooth functions
                on
                = succeed ":" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ∈
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi Alg
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^n)
                      \\;\in\;
                      \\mathbb{R} Alg
                      \\,.
              %p If
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi n
                            %mn 1
                      %mo ⟶
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi n
                            %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      f \;\colon\; \mathbb{R}^{n_1} \longrightarrow \mathbb{R}^{n_2}
              %p
                is any
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+function"} smooth function
                (def.
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CartesianSpacesAndSmoothFunctionsBetweenThem"}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} pre-composition
                with
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                (“
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback+of+functions"}> pullback of functions
                ”)
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mi C
                                %mn ∞
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msup
                                %mi ℝ
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi n
                                    %mn 2
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                              %mover
                                %mo ⟶
                                %mrow
                                  %msup
                                    %mi f
                                    %mo *
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mi C
                                %mn ∞
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msup
                                %mi ℝ
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi n
                                    %mn 1
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi g
                            %mtd
                              %mo ↦
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mi f
                                %mo *
                              %mi g
                              %mo ≔
                              %mi g
                              %mo ∘
                              %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{
                      C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^{n_2})
                      \&amp;\overset{f^\ast}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                      C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^{n_1})
                      \\\
                      g &amp;\mapsto&amp; f^\ast g \coloneqq g \circ f
                      }
              %p
                is an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+algebra"} algebra
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
                in that
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
