                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^\bullet(X)
                for the set of differential forms on the smooth set
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                defined this way.
              %p
                Moreover, given a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+form"} differential k-form
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi ω
                      %msup
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi Ω
                        %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      X \overset{\omega}{\longrightarrow} \mathbf{\Omega}^k
              %p
                on a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+set"} smooth set
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                this way, then its
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+differential"} de Rham differential
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mi ω
                      %mo ∈
                      %msup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mrow
                          %mi k
                          %mo +
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \omega \in \Omega^{k+1}(X)
                is given by the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composite
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+sets"} smooth sets
                with the universal de Rham differential from
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:deRhamDifferentialUniversal"} (23)
              #eq:FormsOnSmoothSetDeRhamDifferential.maruku-equation
                %span.maruku-eq-number (24)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mi ω
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi X
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi ω
                      %msup
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi Ω
                        %mi k
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi d
                      %msup
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi Ω
                        %mrow
                          %mi k
                          %mo +
                          %mn 1
