                      \\,.
              %p
                In particular this means that restricted to the prolonged shell
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℰ
                        %mn ∞
                      %mo ↪
                      %msubsup
                        %mi J
                        %mi Σ
                        %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}^\infty \hookrightarrow J^\infty_\Sigma(E)
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:ProlongedShellInJetBundle"} (52)
                the total spacetime derivative of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presymplectic+current"} presymplectic current
                vanishes:
              #eq:HorizontalDerivativeOfPresymplecticCurrentVanishesOnShell.maruku-equation
                %span.maruku-eq-number (58)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %msub
                        %mi Ω
                        %mi BFV
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi ℰ
                            %mn ∞
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo =
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mn 0
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      d \Omega_{BFV} \vert_{\mathcal{E}^\infty} \;=\; 0
                      \\,.
            .proof
              %h6#proof_2 Proof
              %p
                By prop.
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EulerLagrangeOperatorForTivialVectorBundleOverMinkowskiSpacetime"}
                we have
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi δ
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi L
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi δ
                        %mi EL
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi L
                      %mo −
                      %mi d
                      %msub
                        %mi Θ
                        %mi BFV
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\delta \mathbf{L} = \delta_{EL} \mathbf{L} - d \Theta_{BFV}
                      \\,.
              %p
                The claim follows from applying the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/variational+derivative"} variational derivative
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi δ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta
                to both sides, using
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:HorizontalAndVerticalDerivativeAnticommute"} (37)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi δ
                        %mn 2
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta^2 = 0
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi δ
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi d
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mi d
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi δ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta \circ d = - d \circ \delta
            %p
              Many examples of interest fall into the following two special cases of prop.
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EulerLagrangeOperatorForTivialVectorBundleOverMinkowskiSpacetime"}
            #ShellForSpacetimeIndependentLagrangians.num_prop
              %h6#example_8 Example
              %p
                %strong
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euler-Lagrange+form"} Euler-Lagrange form
                  for
                  = succeed "-independent" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+densities"} Lagrangian densities
              %p
                Let
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi E
                      %mo ,
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi L
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (E,\mathbf{L})
                be a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+field+theory"} Lagrangian field theory
                (def.
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocalLagrangianDensityOnSecondOrderJetBundleOfTrivialVectorBundleOverMinkowskiSpacetime"}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+bundle"} field bundle
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trivial+vector+bundle"} trivial vector bundle
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi Σ
                      %mo ×
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \simeq \Sigma \times F
                over
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
                (example
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TrivialVectorBundleAsAFieldBundle"}
              %p
                In general the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+density"} Lagrangian density
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi L
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{L}
                is a function of all the spacetime and field coordinates
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi L
                      %mo =
                      %mi L
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi x
                        %mi μ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msubsup
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mrow
                          %mo ,
                          %mi μ
                        %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ⋯
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %msub
                        %mi dvol
                        %mi Σ
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\mathbf{L} = L((x^\mu), (\phi^a), (\phi^a_{,\mu}), \cdots) dvol_\Sigma
                      \\,.
              %p
                Consider the special case that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi L
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{L}
                is
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"}> spacetime
                  \-independent
                in that the Lagrangian function
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi L
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
                is independent of the spacetime coordinate
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi x
                          %mi μ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x^\mu)
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euler-Lagrange+form"} Euler-Lagrange form
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi δ
                        %mi EL
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi L
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta_{EL}\mathbf{L}
                (prop.
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EulerLagrangeOperatorForTivialVectorBundleOverMinkowskiSpacetime"}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shell"} shell
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:ProlongedShellInJetBundle"} (52)
                is itself a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trivial+bundle"} trivial bundle
                over spacetime.
              %p
                In this situation every point
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi φ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varphi
                in the jet fiber defines a constant section of the shell:
              #eq:ConstantSectionOfTrivialShellBundle.maruku-equation
                %span.maruku-eq-number (59)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Σ
                      %mo ×
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mi φ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mo ⊂
                      %msup
                        %mi ℰ
                        %mn ∞
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\Sigma \times \{\varphi\} \subset \mathcal{E}^\infty
                      \\,.
            #CanonicalMomentum.num_example
              %h6#example_9 Example
              %p
                %strong
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/canonical+momentum"}> canonical momentum
                  )
              %p
                Consider a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+field+theory"} Lagrangian field theory
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi E
                      %mo ,
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi L
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (E, \mathbf{L})
                (def.
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocalLagrangianDensityOnSecondOrderJetBundleOfTrivialVectorBundleOverMinkowskiSpacetime"}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+density"} Lagrangian density
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi L
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{L}
              %ol
                %li
                  %p
                    does not depend on the
                    = succeed "-" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coordinates"} coordinates
                    (example
                    = succeed ");" do
                      %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ShellForSpacetimeIndependentLagrangians"}
                %li
                  %p
                    depends on spacetime derivatives of
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} field
                    coordinates (hence on
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/jet+bundle"} jet bundle
                    coordinates) at most to first order.
              %p
                Hence if the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+bundle"} field bundle
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mi fb
                      %mi Σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \overset{fb}{\to} \Sigma
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trivial+vector+bundle"} trivial vector bundle
                over
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
                (example
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TrivialVectorBundleAsAFieldBundle"}
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi L
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo =
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi L
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi ϕ
                          %mi a
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ,
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msubsup
                          %mi ϕ
                          %mrow
                            %mo ,
                            %mi μ
                          %mi a
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo )
                      %mo ∧
                      %msub
                        %mi dvol
                        %mi Σ
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\mathbf{L}
                      \\;=\;
                      L\left(
                      (\phi^a), (\phi^a_{,\mu})
                      \\right) \wedge dvol_\Sigma
                      \\,.
              %p
                Then the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presymplectic+current"} presymplectic current
                (def.
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EulerLagrangeOperatorForTivialVectorBundleOverMinkowskiSpacetime"}
              #eq:CanonicalMomentumPresymplecticCurrent.maruku-equation
                %span.maruku-eq-number (60)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Ω
                        %mi BFV
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo =
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi δ
                      %msubsup
                        %mi p
                        %mi a
                        %mi μ
                      %mo ∧
                      %mi δ
                      %msup
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mi a
                      %mo ∧
                      %msub
                        %mi ι
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mo ∂
                            %mi μ
                      %msub
                        %mi dvol
                        %mi Σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\Omega_{BFV}
                      \\;=\;
                      \\delta p_a^\mu
                      \\wedge
                      \\delta \phi^a
                      \\wedge
                      \\iota_{\partial_\mu} dvol_\Sigma
              %p where
              #eq:CanonicalMomentumInCoordinates.maruku-equation
                %span.maruku-eq-number (61)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi p
                        %mi a
                        %mi μ
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ≔
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mfrac
                        %mrow
                          %mo ∂
                          %mi L
                        %mrow
                          %mo ∂
                          %msubsup
                            %mi ϕ
                            %mrow
                              %mo ,
                              %mi μ
                            %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      p_a^\mu
                      \\;\coloneqq\;
                      \\frac{\partial L}{ \partial \phi^a_{,\mu}}
              %p
                denotes the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partial+derivative"} partial derivative
                of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+density"} Lagrangian function
                with respect to the spacetime-
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivatives"} derivatives
                of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} field
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coordinates"} coordinates
              %p Here
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi p
                                %mi a
                            %mtd
                              %mo ≔
                              %msubsup
                                %mi p
                                %mi a
                                %mn 0
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo =
                              %mfrac
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∂
                                  %mi L
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∂
                                  %msubsup
                                    %mi ϕ
                                    %mrow
                                      %mo ,
                                      %mn 0
                                    %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\begin{aligned}
                      p_a
                      \&amp; \coloneqq
                      p_a^0
                      \\\
                      \&amp; =
                      \\frac{\partial L}{\partial \phi^a_{,0}}
                      \\end{aligned}
              %p
                is called the
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/canonical+momentum"} canonical momentum
                corresponding to the “
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/canonical+coordinate"}> canonical field coordinate
                ”
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi ϕ
                          %mi a
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi^a
              %p
                In the language of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multisymplectic+geometry"} multisymplectic geometry
                the full expression
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi p
                        %mi a
                        %mi μ
                      %mo ∧
                      %msub
                        %mi ι
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mo ∂
                            %mi μ
                      %msub
                        %mi dvol
                        %mi Σ
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ∈
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mi Σ
                        %mrow
                          %mi p
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      p_a^\mu \wedge \iota_{\partial_\mu} dvol_\Sigma
                      \\;\in\;
                      \\Omega^{p,1}_\Sigma(E)
              %p is also called the “canonical multi-momentum”, or similar.
            .proof
              %h6#proof_3 Proof
              %p We compute:
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi d
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi L
                            %mtd
                              %mo =
                              %mrow
                                %mo (
                                %mfrac
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo ∂
                                    %mi L
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo ∂
                                    %msup
                                      %mi ϕ
                                      %mi a
                                %mi δ
                                %msup
                                  %mi ϕ
                                  %mi a
                                %mo +
                                %mfrac
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo ∂
                                    %mi L
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo ∂
                                    %msubsup
                                      %mi ϕ
                                      %mrow
                                        %mo ,
                                        %mi μ
                                      %mi a
                                %mi δ
                                %msubsup
                                  %mi ϕ
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo ,
                                    %mi μ
                                  %mi a
                                %mo )
                              %mi δ
                              %msup
                                %mi ϕ
                                %mi a
                              %mo ∧
                              %msub
                                %mi dvol
                                %mi Σ
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo =
                              %mrow
                                %mo (
                                %mfrac
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo ∂
                                    %mi L
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo ∂
                                    %msup
                                      %mi ϕ
                                      %mi a
                                %mo −
                                %mfrac
                                  %mi d
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi d
                                    %msup
                                      %mi x
                                      %mi μ
                                %mfrac
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo ∂
                                    %mi L
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo ∂
                                    %msubsup
                                      %mi ϕ
                                      %mrow
                                        %mo ,
                                        %mi μ
                                      %mi a
                                %mo )
                              %mo ∧
                              %msub
                                %mi dvol
                                %mi Σ
                              %mo −
                              %mi d
                              %munder
                                %munder
                                  %mrow
                                    %mrow
                                      %mo (
                                      %mfrac
                                        %mrow
                                          %mo ∂
                                          %mi L
                                        %mrow
                                          %mo ∂
                                          %msubsup
                                            %mi ϕ
                                            %mrow
                                              %mo ,
                                              %mi μ
                                            %mi a
                                      %mi δ
                                      %msup
                                        %mi ϕ
                                        %mi a
                                      %mo )
                                    %mo ∧
                                    %msub
                                      %mi ι
                                      %mrow
                                        %msub
                                          %mo ∂
                                          %mi μ
                                    %msub
                                      %mi dvol
                                      %mi Σ
                                  %mo ⏟
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi Θ
                                    %mi BFV
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\begin{aligned}
                      \\mathbf{d} \mathbf{L}
                      \&amp; =
                      \\left(
                      \\frac{\partial L}{\partial \phi^a} \delta \phi^a
                      +
                      \\frac{\partial L}{\partial \phi^a_{,\mu}} \delta \phi^a_{,\mu}
                      \\right)
                      \\delta \phi^a
                      \\wedge
                      dvol_\Sigma
                      \\\
                      \&amp; =
                      \\left(
                      \\frac{\partial L}{\partial \phi^a}
                      \-
                      \\frac{d}{d x^\mu} \frac{\partial L}{\partial \phi^a_{,\mu}}
                      \\right)
                      \\wedge
                      dvol_\Sigma
                      \-
                      d
                      \\underset{
                      \\Theta_{BFV}
                      }{
                      \\underbrace{
                      \\left(
                      \\frac{\partial L}{\partial \phi^a_{,\mu}} \delta \phi^a
                      \\right)
                      \\wedge
                      \\iota_{\partial_\mu} dvol_\Sigma
                      }
                      }
                      \\end{aligned}
                      \\,.
              %p Hence
