                = succeed "," do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PresymplecticCurrentDiracField"}
              #eq:RecallPresymplecticCurrentOfDiracField.maruku-equation
                %span.maruku-eq-number (85)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Ω
                        %mi BFV
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo =
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mover
                        %mrow
                          %mi δ
                          %mi ψ
                        %mo ¯
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %msup
                        %mi γ
                        %mi μ
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi δ
                      %mi ψ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %msub
                        %mi ι
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mo ∂
                            %mi μ
                      %msub
                        %mi dvol
                        %mi Σ
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\Omega_{BFV}
                      \\;=\;
                      (\overline{\delta \psi}) \, \gamma^\mu \, (\delta \psi) \, \iota_{\partial_\mu} dvol_\Sigma
                      \\,.
              %p
                Consider this specifically in
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                      %mo =
                      %mn 4
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p + 1 = 4
                in which case the components
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ψ
                        %mi α
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi_\alpha
                are
                = succeed "-valued" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+number"} complex number
                = succeed ")," do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SpacetimeAsMatrices"}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tuple"} tuple
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi ψ
                        %mi α
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\psi_\alpha)
                amounts to 8 real-valued coordinate functions. By changing complex coordinates, we may equivalently consider
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi ψ
                        %mi α
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\psi_\alpha)
                as four coordinate functions, and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mover
                          %mi ψ
                          %mo ¯
                        %mi α
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\overline{\psi}^\alpha)
                as another four independent coordinate functions.
              %p
                Using this coordinate transformation, it is immediate to find the following
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pairs"} pairs
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hamiltonian+vector+fields"} Hamiltonian vector fields
                and their
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hamiltonian+differential+forms"} Hamiltonian differential forms
                from def.
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HamiltonianForms"}
                applied to
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:RecallPresymplecticCurrentOfDiracField"} (85)
              %table
                %thead
                  %tr
                    %th
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hamiltonian+vector+field"} Hamiltonian vector field
                    %th
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hamiltonian+differential+form"} Hamiltonian differential form
                %tbody
                  %tr
                    %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mphantom
                              %mi AA
                            %msub
                              %mo ∂
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi ψ
                                  %mi α
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phantom{AA} \partial_{\psi_\alpha}
                    %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mphantom
                              %mi AA
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                                %mo (
                                %mover
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi δ
                                    %mi ψ
                                  %mo ¯
                                %msup
                                  %mi γ
                                  %mi μ
                                %mo )
                              %mi α
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %msub
                              %mi ι
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mo ∂
                                  %mi μ
                            %msub
                              %mi dvol
                              %mi Σ
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phantom{AA}\left(\overline{\delta \psi}\gamma^\mu\right)^\alpha\, \iota_{\partial_\mu} dvol_\Sigma
                  %tr
                    %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mphantom
                              %mi AA
                            %msub
                              %mo ∂
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mover
                                    %mi ψ
                                    %mo ¯
                                  %mi α
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phantom{AA} \partial_{\overline{\psi}_\alpha}
                    %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mphantom
                              %mi AA
                            %msub
                              %mrow
                                %mo (
                                %msup
                                  %mi γ
                                  %mi μ
                                %mi ψ
                                %mo )
                              %mi α
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %msub
                              %mi ι
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mo ∂
                                  %mi μ
                            %msub
                              %mi dvol
                              %mi Σ
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phantom{AA}\left( \gamma^\mu \psi  \right)_\alpha \, \iota_{\partial_\mu} dvol_\Sigma
              %p
                and to obtain the following non-trivial
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+bracket+Lie+n-algebra"} local Poisson brackets
                (prop.
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocalPoissonBracket"}
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mo {
                        %msub
                          %mrow
                            %mo (
                            %msup
                              %mi γ
                              %mi μ
                            %mi ψ
                            %mo )
                          %mi α
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %msub
                          %mi ι
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mo ∂
                              %mi μ
                        %msub
                          %mi dvol
                          %mi Σ
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ,
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %msup
                          %mrow
                            %mo (
                            %mover
                              %mi ψ
                              %mo ¯
                            %msup
                              %mi γ
                              %mi μ
                            %mo )
                          %mi β
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %msub
                          %mi ι
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mo ∂
                              %mi μ
                        %msub
                          %mi dvol
                          %mi Σ
                        %mo }
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo =
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msub
                        %mrow
                          %mo (
                          %msup
                            %mi γ
                            %mi μ
                          %mo )
                        %mi α
                      %msup
                        %mrow
                        %mi β
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %msub
                        %mi ι
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mo ∂
                            %mi μ
                      %msub
                        %mi dvol
                        %mi Σ
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\left\{
                      \\left( \gamma^\mu \psi  \right)_\alpha \, \iota_{\partial_\mu} dvol_\Sigma
                      \\,,\,
                      \\left(\overline{\psi}\gamma^\mu\right)^\beta\, \iota_{\partial_\mu} dvol_\Sigma
                      \\right\}
                      \\;=\;
                      \\left(\gamma^\mu\right)_\alpha{}^{\beta} \, \iota_{\partial_\mu} dvol_\Sigma
                      \\,.
              %p
                Notice the signs: Due to the odd-grading of the field coordinate function
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ψ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi δ
                      %mi ψ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta \psi
                has bi-degree
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi odd
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (1,odd)
                and the contraction operation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ι
                        %mi ψ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \iota_{\psi}
                has bi-degree
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi odd
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-1,odd)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi ψ
                        %mo ¯
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{\psi}
                picks up
                %em two
                minus signs, a “cohomological” sign due to the differential form degrees, and a “supergeometric” one (def.
                = succeed "):" do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DifferentialFormOnSuperCartesianSpaces"}
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ι
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mo ∂
                            %mi ψ
                      %mover
                        %mrow
                          %mi δ
                          %mi ψ
                        %mo ¯
                      %mi ⋯
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mover
                        %mrow
                          %mi δ
                          %mi ψ
                        %mo ¯
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %msub
                        %mi ι
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mo ∂
                            %mi ψ
                      %mi ⋯
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\iota_{\partial_\psi} \overline{\delta \psi} \cdots
                      \=
                      (-1) (-1) \overline{\delta \psi} \,\iota_{\partial_\psi} \cdots
                      \\,.
              %p
                For the same reason, the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+bracket+Lie+n-algebra"} local Poisson bracket
                is a
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+algebra"} super Lie algebra
                with
                %em symmetric
                super Lie bracket:
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mo {
                        %msub
                          %mrow
                            %mo (
                            %msup
                              %mi γ
                              %mi μ
                            %mi ψ
                            %mo )
                          %mi α
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %msub
                          %mi ι
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mo ∂
                              %mi μ
                        %msub
                          %mi dvol
                          %mi Σ
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ,
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %msup
                          %mrow
                            %mo (
                            %mover
                              %mi ψ
                              %mo ¯
                            %msup
                              %mi γ
                              %mi μ
                            %mo )
                          %mi β
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %msub
                          %mi ι
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mo ∂
                              %mi μ
                        %msub
                          %mi dvol
                          %mi Σ
                        %mo }
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo =
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo +
                      %mrow
                        %mo {
                        %msup
                          %mrow
                            %mo (
                            %mover
                              %mi ψ
                              %mo ¯
                            %msup
                              %mi γ
                              %mi μ
                            %mo )
                          %mi β
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %msub
                          %mi ι
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mo ∂
                              %mi μ
                        %msub
                          %mi dvol
                          %mi Σ
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ,
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %msub
                          %mrow
                            %mo (
                            %msup
                              %mi γ
                              %mi μ
                            %mi ψ
                            %mo )
                          %mi α
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %msub
                          %mi ι
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mo ∂
                              %mi μ
                        %msub
                          %mi dvol
                          %mi Σ
                        %mo }
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\left\{
                      \\left( \gamma^\mu \psi  \right)_\alpha \, \iota_{\partial_\mu} dvol_\Sigma
                      \\,,\,
                      \\left(\overline{\psi}\gamma^\mu\right)^\beta\, \iota_{\partial_\mu} dvol_\Sigma
                      \\right\}
                      \\;=\;
                      +
                      \\left\{
                      \\left(\overline{\psi}\gamma^\mu\right)^\beta\, \iota_{\partial_\mu} dvol_\Sigma
                      \\,,\,
                      \\left( \gamma^\mu \psi  \right)_\alpha \, \iota_{\partial_\mu} dvol_\Sigma
                      \\right\}
                      \\,.
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
            %p
              This concludes our discussion of general
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+symmetries+of+a+Lagrangian"} infinitesimal symmetries of a Lagrangian
              %em
                %a{:href => "#GaugeSymmetries"} Gauge symmetries
              below. First, in the
              %a{:href => "#Observables"} next chapter
              we discuss the concept of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/observables"} observables
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+theory"} field theory
          %div
            %h2#Observables Observables
            %p In this chapter we discuss these topics:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %em
                    %a{:href => "#GeneralObservables"} General observables
              %li
                %p
                  %em
                    %a{:href => "#LinearOffShellObservablesAreDistributions"} Polynomial off-shell observables and Distributions
              %li
                %p
                  %em
                    %a{:href => "#PolynomialOnShellObservablesAreDistributionalSolutionsToTheEquationsOfMotion"} Polynomial on-shell observables and Distributional solutions to PDEs
              %li
                %p
                  %em
                    %a{:href => "#LocalObservablesByTransgression"} Local observables and Transgression
              %li
                %p
                  %em
                    %a{:href => "#InfinitesimalObservables"} Infinitesimal observables
              %li
                %p
                  %em
                    %a{:href => "#StatesArePositiveLinearFunctionals"} States
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
            %p
              Given a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+field+theory"} Lagrangian field theory
              (def.
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LagrangianForFreeScalarFieldOnMinkowskiSpacetime"}
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/observable"} observable
                quantity
              or just
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/observable"} observable
              for short (def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Observable"}
              below), is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+function"} smooth function
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mi Σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi δ
                          %mi EL
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi L
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi ℂ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    A \;\colon\; \Gamma_\Sigma(E)_{\delta_{EL}\mathbf{L} = 0} \longrightarrow \mathbb{C}
            %p
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/on-shell"} on-shell
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space+of+field+histories"} space of field histories
              (example
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DiffeologicalSpaceOfFieldHistories"}
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SupergeometricSpaceOfFieldHistories"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+function"} smooth
              “
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functional"}> functional
              ” of field histories. We think of this as assigning to each physically realizable field history
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Φ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi
              the value
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Φ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A(\Phi)
              of the given quantity as exhibited by that field history. For instance concepts like “average
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+strength"} field strength
              in the compact spacetime region
              = succeed "\u201D" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒪
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}
              %em
                field
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/amplitude"} amplitude
                at spacetime point
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              should be an observable, the “
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+observable"}> field observable
              ” denoted
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi Φ
                        %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{\Phi}^a(x)
            %p
              Beware that in much of the literature on
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+theory"} field theory
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+observables"} field observables
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Φ
                      %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{\Phi}^a(x)
              (example below
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PointEvaluationObservables"}
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/types"} types
                  of fields/
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+bundles"} field bundles
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi E
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+histories"}> field histories
                  \/
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sections"} sections
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Φ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functions"} functions
                  on the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space+of+field+histories"} space of field histories
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi Φ
                            %mi a
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{\Phi}^a(x)
            %p
              In particular, the process of
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantization"} quantization
              (discussed in
              %em
                %a{:href => "#Quantization"} Quantization
              below) affects the third of these concepts only, in that it
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/deformation+theory"} deforms
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+algebra"} algebra
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure"} structure
              on observables to a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-commutative+algebra"} non-commutative
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+of+quantum+observables"} algebra of quantum observables
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+observables"} field observables
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Φ
                      %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{\Phi}^a(x)
              are often referred to as
              = succeed "." do
                %em quantum fields
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} quantum field theory
              it is important that the
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Φ
