                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+future+cone"} closed future cone
                of the origin.
            %p
            #CausalPropagatorIsSkewSymmetric.num_prop
              %h6 Proposition
              %p
                %strong
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/causal+propagator"} causal propagator
                  is skew-symmetric)
                %br/
                Under reversal of arguments the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/advanced+and+retarded+causal+propagators"} advanced and retarded causal propagators
                from prop.
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AdvancedRetardedPropagatorsForKleinGordonOnMinkowskiSpacetime"}
                are related by
              #eq:AdvancedAndRetardedPropagatorTurnIntoEachOtherUnderSwitchingArguments.maruku-equation
                %span.maruku-eq-number (144)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Δ
                        %mo ±
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi y
                      %mo −
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi Δ
                        %mo ∓
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo −
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\Delta_{\pm}(y-x) = \Delta_\mp(x-y)
                      \\,.
              %p
                It follows that the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/causal+propagator"} causal propagator
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:CausalPropagator"} (95)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo ≔
                      %msub
                        %mi Δ
                        %mo +
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %msub
                        %mi Δ
                        %mo −
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta \coloneqq \Delta_+ - \Delta_-
                is skew-symmetric in its arguments:
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo −
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %msub
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi y
                      %mo −
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\Delta_S(x-y) = - \Delta_S(y-x)
                      \\,.
              %p
