              %p
                We further discuss these
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+gauge+transformations"} higher gauge transformations
                below.
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
            %p#LieAlgebraActionAndLieAlgebroids
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+actions"} Lie algebra actions
                and
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebroids"} Lie algebroids
            %p
              We have seen above
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+gauge+symmetries"} infinitesimal gauge symmetries
              %em implied
              by a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+field+theory"} Lagrangian field theory
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+symmetries+of+the+Lagrangian"} infinitesimal symmetries of the Lagrangian
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/obstructions"} obstructions
              that these
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+gauge+symmetries"} infinitesimal gauge symmetries
              cause for the existence of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covariant+phase+space"} covariant phase space
              (via prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#NonTrivialImplicitInfinitesimalGaugeSymmetriesPbstructExistenceOfCauchySurfaces"}
              and remark
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GaugeParametrizedInfinitesimalGaugeTransformation"}
              = succeed ")" do
                %em
                  %a{:href => "#GaugeFixing"} Gauge fixing
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type"} type
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} fields
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+quotient"} homotopy quotient
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/jet+bundle"} jet bundle
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+bundle"} field bundle
              by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
              of the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+gauge+symmetries"} infinitesimal gauge symmetries
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+Lie+algebroid"} action Lie algebroid
            %p
              Here we introduce the required
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+Lie+theory"} higher Lie theory
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+%E2%88%9E-algebroids"} Lie ∞-algebroids
              (def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LInfinityAlgebroid"}
              below). Further
              %a{:href => "#BRSTComplex"} below
              we specify this to actions by
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+gauge+symmetries"} infinitesimal gauge symmetries
              to obtain the
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+BRST+complex"} local
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BRST+complex"} BRST complex
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+field+theory"} Lagrangian field theory
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocalOffShellBRSTComplex"}
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
            %p
              The following discussion introduces and uses the tremendously useful fact that (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+Lie+theory"}> higher
              )
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+theory"} Lie theory
              may usefully be dually expressed in terms of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+graded-commutative+algebra"} differential graded-commutative algebra
              (def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#differentialgradedcommutativeSuperalgebra"}
              below), namely in terms of “
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebras"}> Chevalley-Eilenberg algebras
              ”. In the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physics"} physics
              literature, besides the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BRST-BV+formalism"} BRST-BV formalism
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%27Auria-Fr%C3%A9+formulation+of+supergravity"} D'Auria-Fré formulation of supergravity
              (“
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FDAs"}> FDAs
              ”, see the convoluted
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "L-infinity-algebra#History"} history of the concept
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Koszul+duality"} Koszul duality
              between the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+operad"} Lie operad
              and the
              = succeed "\u201D," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+algebra+operad"} commutative algebra operad
            %p
              Before we proceed, we make explicit a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure"} structure
