              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/off-shell"} off-shell
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/jet+bundle"} jet bundle
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+bundle"} field bundle
              and the corresponding
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+quotient"} homotopy quotient
              exhibited by the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+BRST+complex"} local BRST complex
              %a{:href => "#ReducedPhaseSpace"} next chapter
              we discuss the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+intersection"} homotopy intersection
              of this construction with the
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shell"} shell
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reduced+phase+space"} reduced phase space
          %div
            %h2#ReducedPhaseSpace Reduced phase space
            %p In this chapter we discuss these topics:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  Global gauge reduction for strictly
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariant"} invariant
                  functions (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functionals"}> action functionals
                  ):
                %ul
                  %li
                    %p
                      %em
                        %a{:href => "#DerivedCriticalLocusInsideLieAlgebroids"} Derived critical loci inside Lie algebroids
                  %li
                    %p
                      %em
                        %a{:href => "#SchoutenBracketAntibracket"} Schouten bracket on Lie algebroids
              %li
                %p
                  Local gauge reduction for weakly invariant local functions (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+densities"}> Lagrangian densities
                  ):
                %ul
                  %li
                    %p
                      %em
                        %a{:href => "#LocalJetBundleAntibracket"} Local antibracket
                  %li
                    %p
                      %em
                        %a{:href => "#DerivedCriticalLocusOnJetBundle"} Local BV-BRST complex
                  %li
                    %p
                      %em
                        %a{:href => "#BVBRSTComplexGlobal"} Global BV-BRST complex
            %p
              For a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+field+theory"} Lagrangian field theory
              with
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+gauge+symmetries"} infinitesimal gauge symmetries
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reduced+phase+space"} reduced phase space
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient"} quotient
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shell"} shell
              (the
              = succeed "-locus" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/solution"} solution
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equations+of+motion"} equations of motion
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
              of the
              = succeed ";" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+symmetries"} gauge symmetries
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+quotient"} homotopy quotient
              by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+symmetries"} gauge symmetries
              and its
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+intersection"} homotopy intersection
              with the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shell"} shell
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reduced+phase+space"} reduced phase space
              may lift the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/obstruction"} obstruction
              for a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+theory"} gauge theory
              to have a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covariant+phase+space"} covariant phase space
              and hence a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantization"} quantization
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+differential+geometry"} higher differential geometry
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+quotients"} homotopy quotients
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+intersections"} homotopy intersections
              is usefully modeled by tools from
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homological+algebra"} homological algebra
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BV-BRST+complex"} BV-BRST complex
            %p
              In order to exhibit the key structure without getting distracted by the local
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/jet+bundle"} jet bundle
              geometry, we first discuss the simple form in which the reduced phase space would appear after
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transgression+of+variational+differential+forms"} transgression
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TransgressionOfVariationalDifferentialFormsToConfigrationSpaces"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
              were
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+space"} compact
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principle+of+extremal+action"} principle of extremal action
              (prop.
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PrincipleOfExtremalAction"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+critical+locus"} derived critical locus
              (
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mi S
                    %mo ≃
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d S \simeq 0
              ) of a globally defined
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functional"} action functional
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BV-BRST+complex"} BV-BRST complex
              is example
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ArchetypeOfBVBRSTComplex"}
              below.
            %p
              The genuine
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+field+theory"} local
              construction of the derived
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shell"} shell
              is in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/jet+bundle"} jet bundle
              of the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+bundle"} field bundle
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functional"} action functional
              appears “de-transgressed” in the form of the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+density"} Lagrangian density
              %em local
              incarnation of the redcuced phase space is modeled by the genuine
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+BV-BRST+complex"} local BV-BRST complex
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocalBVBRSTComplexIsDerivedCriticalLocusOfEulerLagrangeForm"}
              below.
            %p
              Finally, under
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transgression+of+variational+differential+forms"} transgression of variational differential forms
              this yields a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential"} differential
              on the graded
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+observables"} local observables
              of the field theory. This is the
              %em
                global
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BV-BRST+complex"} BV-BRST complex
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+field+theory"} Lagrangian field theory
              (def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ComplexBVBRSTGlobal"}
              below).
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
            %p#DerivedCriticalLocusInsideLieAlgebroids
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+critical+loci"} derived critical loci
                inside
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebroids"} Lie algebroids
            %p
              By analogy with the algebraic formulation of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+functions"} smooth functions
              between
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+spaces"} Cartesian spaces
              (the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/embedding+of+smooth+manifolds+into+formal+duals+of+R-algebras"} embedding of Cartesian spaces into formal duals of R-algebras
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AlgebraicFactsOfDifferentialGeometry"}
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebroids"} Lie algebroids
            #HomomorphismBetweenLieAlgebroids.num_defn
              %h6#definition Definition
              %p
                %strong
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
                  between
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebroids"} Lie algebroids
              %p
                Given two
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+Lie+algebroids"} derived Lie algebroids
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝔞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{a}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝔞
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{a}'
                (def.
                = succeed ")," do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LInfinityAlgebroid"}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
                between them
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi 𝔞
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi 𝔞
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      f \;\colon\; \mathfrak{a} \longrightarrow \mathfrak{a}'
              %p
                is a
                = succeed "-" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-algebra"} dg-algebra
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
                between their
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebras"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebras
                going the other way around
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi CE
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝔞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⟵
                      %mi CE
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝔞
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      CE(\mathfrak{a}) \longleftarrow CE(\mathfrak{a}') \;\colon\; f^\ast
              %p such that this covers an algebra homomorphism on the function algebras:
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi CE
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi 𝔞
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                              %mover
                                %mo ⟵
                                %mrow
                                  %msup
                                    %mi f
                                    %mo *
                            %mtd
                              %mi CE
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi 𝔞
                              %mo ′
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mi C
                                %mn ∞
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi X
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                              %munder
                                %mo ⟵
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi f
                                  %msub
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                    %mi X
                                  %msup
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                    %mo *
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mi C
                                %mn ∞
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi Y
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{
                      CE(\mathfrak{a}) &amp;\overset{f^\ast}{\longleftarrow}&amp; CE(\mathfrak{a}')
                      \\\
                      \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                      \\\
                      C^\infty(X) &amp;\underset{(f\vert_X)^\ast}{\longleftarrow}&amp; C^\infty(Y)
                      }
                      \\,.
              %p
                (This is also called a “
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curved+sh-map"}> non-curved sh-map
                ”.)
            #GaugeInvariantFunctionsIntermsOfLieAlgebroids.num_example
              %h6#example Example
              %p
                %strong
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariant"} invariant
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functions"} functions
                  in terms of
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebroids"} Lie algebroids
              %p
                Let
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝔤
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
                be a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+algebra"} super Lie algebra
                equipped with a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+action"} Lie algebra action
                (def.
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#InfinitesimalActionByLieAlgebra"}
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi 𝔤
                              %mo ×
                              %mi X
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mover
                                %mo ⟶
                                %mi R
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mi T
                              %mi X
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mrow
                                %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                  %mrow
                                    %msub
                                      %mi pr
                                      %mn 2
                              %mo ↘
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mo ↙
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mi rb
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{
                      \\mathfrak{g} \times X &amp;&amp; \overset{R}{\longrightarrow} &amp;&amp; T X
                      \\\
                      \&amp; {}_{\mathllap{pr_2}}\searrow &amp;&amp; \swarrow_{\mathrlap{rb}}
                      \\\
                      \&amp;&amp; X
                      }
              %p
                on a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supermanifold"} supermanifold
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebroids"} Lie algebroids
                (def.
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HomomorphismBetweenLieAlgebroids"}
              #eq:ProjectionMapForActionLieAlgebroid.maruku-equation
                %span.maruku-eq-number (175)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi X
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mi CE
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi X
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                              %mo =
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mi C
                                %mn ∞
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi X
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                              %mo ⊕
                            %mtd
                              %mn 0
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mi p
                            %mtd
                              %mphantom
                                %mi AAA
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mrow
                                    %msup
                                      %mi p
                                      %mo *
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mi id
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mn 0
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi X
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                              %mi 𝔤
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mi CE
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi X
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                              %mi 𝔤
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                              %mo =
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mi C
                                %mn ∞
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi X
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                              %mo ⊕
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mi C
                                %mn ∞
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi X
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo ⊗
                              %msup
                                %mo ∧
                                %mo •
                              %msup
                                %mi 𝔤
                                %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{
                      X &amp;&amp;&amp; CE(X) &amp;=&amp; C^\infty(X) &amp;\oplus&amp; 0
                      \\\
                      \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{p}}
                      \&amp;\phantom{AAA}&amp;&amp;
                      \\uparrow^{\mathrlap{p^\ast}}
                      \&amp;&amp;
                      \\uparrow^{\mathrlap{id}} &amp;&amp; \uparrow^{\mathrlap{0}}
                      \\\
                      X/\mathfrak{g}
                      \&amp;&amp;&amp;
                      CE(X/\mathfrak{g})
                      \&amp;=&amp;
                      C^\infty(X)
                      \&amp;\oplus&amp;
                      C^\infty(X) \otimes \wedge^\bullet \mathfrak{g}^\ast
                      }
              %p
                from the manifold
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                regarded as a Lie algebroid by example
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#BasicExamplesOfLieAlgebroids"}
                to the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+Lie+algebroid"} action Lie algebroid
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi 𝔤
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X/\mathfrak{g}
                (example
                = succeed ")," do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ActionLieAlgebroid"}
                = succeed "." do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+quotient"} homotopy quotient
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coprojection"} coprojection
                    map
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+graded-commutative+superalgebras"} differential graded-commutative superalgebras
                is given simply by the identity on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(X)
                and the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero+map"} zero map
                on
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi 𝔤
                          %mo *
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}^\ast
              %p
                Next regard the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+line"} real line
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^1
                as a Lie algebroid by example
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#BasicExamplesOfLieAlgebroids"}
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HomomorphismBetweenLieAlgebroids"}
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo ⟶
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mn 1
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ,
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      S \;\colon\; X/\mathfrak{g} \longrightarrow \mathbb{R}^1
                      \\,,
              %p
                hence
                = succeed "," do
                  %em smooth functions on the Lie algebroid
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    ordinary
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+functions"} smooth functions
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
