                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\begin{aligned}
                      0 &amp; =
                      \\left( d_{CE\left( (X/\mathfrak{g})_{d S \simeq 0} \right)} \right)^2
                      \\\
                      \&amp; =
                      \\left( s_{BV} +  s_{BRST}\right)^2
                      \\\
                      \&amp; =
                      \\underset{ = 0 }{
                      \\underbrace{
                      \\left( s_{BV}\right)^2
                      }}
                      +
                      \\underset{ = 0 }{
                      \\underbrace{
                      \\left( s_{BRST} \right)^2
                      }}
                      +
                      \\underset{ = 0 }{
                      \\underbrace{
                      \\left[ s_{BV}, s_{BRST} \right]
                      }
                      }
                      \\end{aligned}
              %p
                all three terms have to vanish separately, as shown, since they each have different bidegree (the last term denotes the graded commutator, hence the
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anticommutator"} anticommutator
              %p
                Notice that the nilpotency of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
