            %p
              So far the discussion yields just the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+of+functions"} algebra of functions
              on the derived reduced prolonged shell. We now discuss the derived analog of the full
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/variational+bicomplex"} variational bicomplex
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#VariationalBicomplexOnSecondOrderJetBundleOverTrivialVectorBundleOverMinkowskiSpacetime"}
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
            %p
              %strong (derived variational bicomplex)
            %p
              The analog of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+complex"} de Rham complex
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+Lie+algebroid"} derived Lie algebroid
              is called the
              = succeed ":" do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Weil+algebra"} Weil algebra
            #WeilAlgebra.num_defn
              %h6#definition_9 Definition
              %p
                %strong
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Weil+algebra"} Weil algebra
                  of a
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebroid"} Lie algebroid
              %p
                Given a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+Lie+algebroid"} derived Lie algebroid
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝔞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{a}
                over some
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                (def.
                = succeed ")," do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LInfinityAlgebroid"}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Weil+algebra"} Weil algebra
                is
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
