                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+density"} Lagrangian density
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi L
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{L}'
                the part independent of
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/antifields"} antifields
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euler-Lagrange+equation"} Euler-Lagrange
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equations+of+motion"} equations of motion
                (def.
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EulerLagrangeEquationsOnTrivialVectorFieldBundleOverMinkowskiSpacetime"}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cauchy+surfaces"} Cauchy surfaces
                (def.
                = succeed ")," do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CauchySurface"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi L
                        %mi gf
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{L}_{gf}
                a
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+fixing+Lagrangian+density"} gauge fixing Lagrangian density
                for the original Lagrangian field theory, and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi L
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{L}'
                the corresponding
                %em gauge fixed
                form of the original
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+density"} Lagrangian density
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi L
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{L}
            .num_remark
              %h6#remark Remark
              %p
                %strong (warning on terminology)
              %p
                What we call a
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+fixing+Lagrangian+density"} gauge fixing Lagrangian density
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi L
                        %mi gf
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{L}_{gf}
                in def.
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GaugeFixingLagrangianDensity"}
                is traditionally called a
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+fixing+fermion"} gauge fixing fermion
                and denoted by “
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ψ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi
                ” (
                %a{:href => "BRST+complex#Henneaux90"}> Henneaux 90, section 8.3, 8.4
                ).
              %p
                Here “fermion” is meant as a reference to the fact that the cohomological degree
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi deg
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi L
                          %mi gf
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} deg(L_{gf}) = -1
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergeometry"} super-degree
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fermion"} fermion
                fields such as the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+field"} Dirac field
                (example
                = succeed ");" do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DiracFieldBundle"}
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/signs+in+supergeometry"} signs in supergeometry
                the section
                = succeed "." do
                  %em
                    %a{:href => "signs+in+supergeometry#SuperOddConvention"} The super odd sign rule
            #GaugeFixingViaAntiLagrangianSubspaces.num_example
              %h6#example Example
              %p
                %strong
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+fixing"} gauge fixing
                  via
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+antibracket"} anti-
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+subspaces"} Lagrangian subspaces
              %p
                Let
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi L
                        %mi gf
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{L}_{gf}
                be a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+fixing+Lagrangian+density"} gauge fixing Lagrangian density
                as in def.
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GaugeFixingLagrangianDensity"}
                such that
              %ol
                %li
                  %p
                    its
                    = succeed "-square" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+antibracket"} local antibracket
                  .maruku-equation
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mrow
                            %mo {
                            %msub
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi L
                              %mi gf
                            %mo ,
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mrow
                              %mo {
                              %msub
                                %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                  %mi L
                                %mi gf
                              %mo ,
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %mo −
                              %mo }
                            %mo }
                          %mo =
                          %mn 0
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                          \\left\{ \mathbf{L}_{gf},\, \left\{ \mathbf{L}_{gf}, \, -\right\} \right\} = 0
                  %p
                    hence its
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+antibracket"} anti-
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hamiltonian+flow"} Hamiltonian flow
                    has at most a linear component in its argument
                    = succeed ":" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi A
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{A}
                  .maruku-equation
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi e
                            %mrow
                              %mo {
                              %msub
                                %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                  %mi L
                                %mi gf
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %mo ,
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi A
                              %mo }
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mo =
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi A
                          %mo +
                          %mrow
                            %mo {
                            %msub
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi L
                              %mi gf
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mo ,
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi A
                            %mo }
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                          e^{\left\{ \mathbf{L}_{gf} \,,\, \mathbf{A}  \right\}}
                          \\;=\;
                          \\mathbf{A} + \left\{ \mathbf{L}_{gf} \,,\, \mathbf{A}  \right\}
                %li
                  %p
                    it is independent of the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/antifields"} antifields
                  .maruku-equation
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi deg
                            %mi af
                          %mrow
                            %mo (
                            %msub
                              %mi L
                              %mi gf
                            %mo )
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mo =
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mn 0
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mo .
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                          deg_{af}\left( L_{gf} \right) \;=\; 0
                          \\,.
              %p Then with
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msup
                            %mi ϕ
                            %mi A
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\phi^A)
                    collectively denoting all the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} field
                    coordinates
                  %p
                    (including the actual fields
                    = succeed "," do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi ϕ
                              %mi a
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi^a
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ghost+fields"} ghost fields
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi c
                            %mi α
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c^\alpha
                    as well as possibly further
                    = succeed ")" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/auxiliary+fields"} auxiliary fields
                %li
                  %p
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msubsup
                            %mi ϕ
                            %mi A
                            %mo ‡
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\phi^\ddagger_A)
                    collectively denoting all the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/antifield"} antifield
                    coordinates
                  %p
                    (includion the antifields
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msubsup
                            %mi ϕ
                            %mi a
                            %mo ‡
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi^\ddagger_a
                    of the actual fields, the antifields
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msubsup
                            %mi c
                            %mi α
                            %mo ‡
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c^\ddagger_\alpha
                    of the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ghost+fields"} ghost fields
                    as well as those of possibly further
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/auxiliary+fields"} auxiliary fields
                    )
              %p we have
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi ϕ
                              %mo ′
                              %msup
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mi A
                            %mtd
                              %mo ≔
                              %msup
                                %mi e
                                %mrow
                                  %mo {
                                  %msub
                                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                      %mi L
                                    %mi gf
                                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                                  %mo ,
                                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                                  %mo −
                                  %mo }
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msup
                                %mi ϕ
                                %mi A
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo =
                              %msup
                                %mi ϕ
                                %mi A
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mphantom
                                %mi A
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi ϕ
                              %mo ′
                              %msubsup
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mi A
                                %mo ‡
                            %mtd
                              %mo ≔
                              %msup
                                %mi e
                                %mrow
                                  %mo {
                                  %msub
                                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                      %mi L
                                    %mi gf
                                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                                  %mo ,
                                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                                  %mo −
                                  %mo }
                              %mrow
                                %mo (
                                %msubsup
                                  %mi ϕ
                                  %mi A
                                  %mo ‡
                                %mo )
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo =
                              %msubsup
                                %mi ϕ
                                %mi A
                                %mo ‡
                              %mo −
                              %mfrac
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mover
                                      %mi δ
                                      %mo ←
                                    %mi EL
                                  %msub
                                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                      %mi L
                                    %mi gf
                                %mrow
                                  %mi δ
                                  %msup
                                    %mi ϕ
                                    %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\begin{aligned}
                      (\phi')^A
                      \&amp; \coloneqq
                      e^{\left\{ \mathbf{L}_{gf}\,,\, - \right\}}(\phi^A)
                      \\\
                      \&amp; = \phi^A
                      \\\
                      \\phantom{A}
                      \\\
                      (\phi')^\ddagger_A
                      \&amp; \coloneqq
                      e^{\left\{ \mathbf{L}_{gf}\,,\, - \right\}}
                      \\left( \phi^\ddagger_A \right)
                      \\\
                      \&amp;  =
                      \\phi^\ddagger_A - \frac{\overset{\leftarrow}{\delta}_{EL} \mathbf{L}_{gf}}{\delta \phi^a}
                      \\end{aligned}
              %p
                (and similarly for the higher jets); and the corresponding transformed
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+density"} Lagrangian density
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:GaugeFixedLagrangianDensity"} (199)
                may be written as
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo −
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi L
                              %mo ′
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi L
                              %msub
                                %mo ′
                                %mi BRST
                            %mtd
                              %mo ≔
                              %msup
                                %mi e
                                %mrow
                                  %mo {
                                  %msub
                                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                      %mi L
                                    %mi gf
                                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                                  %mo ,
                                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                                  %mo −
                                  %mo }
                              %mrow
                                %mo (
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                  %mi L
                                %mo +
                                %msub
                                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                    %mi L
                                  %mi BRST
                                %mo )
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo =
                              %mrow
                                %mo (
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                  %mi L
                                %mo +
                                %msub
                                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                    %mi L
                                  %mi BRST
                                %mo )
                              %mrow
                                %mo (
                                %mi ϕ
                                %mo ′
                                %mo ,
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi ϕ
                                %mo ′
                                %msup
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                  %mo ‡
                                %mo )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ,
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\begin{aligned}
                      \-\mathbf{L}' +  \mathbf{L}'_{BRST}
                      \&amp; \coloneqq
                      e^{\left\{ \mathbf{L}_{gf}\,,\, - \right\}}\left( -\mathbf{L} + \mathbf{L}_{BRST} \right)
                      \\\
                      \&amp; =
                      \\left(
                      \-\mathbf{L}
                      +
                      \\mathbf{L}_{BRST}
                      \\right)
                      \\left( \phi', (\phi')^\ddagger  \right)
                      \\end{aligned}
                      \\,,
              %p
                where the notation on the right denotes that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi'
                is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/substitution"} substituted
                for
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϕ
                      %msub
                        %mo ′
                        %mo ‡
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi'_\ddagger
                for
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ϕ
                          %mo ‡
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi_\ddagger
              %p
                This means that the defining condition that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi L
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{L}'
                be the antifield-independent summand
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:GaugeFixedLagrangianDensity"} (199)
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi L
                      %mo ′
                      %mo ≔
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi L
                        %mo +
                        %msub
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi L
                          %mi BRST
                        %mo )
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mo ′
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi ϕ
                          %mo ‡
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                        %mo )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\mathbf{L}'
                      \\coloneqq
                      \\left(
                      \-\mathbf{L}
                      +
                      \\mathbf{L}_{BRST}
                      \\right)
                      \\left( \phi'(\phi), \phi_\ddagger = 0  \right)
              %p translates into
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi L
                      %mo ′
                      %mo ≔
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi L
                        %mo +
                        %msub
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi L
                          %mi BRST
                        %mo )
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mo ′
                        %mo ,
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mo ′
                        %msubsup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi A
                          %mo ‡
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mfrac
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mover
                                %mi δ
                                %mo ←
                              %mi EL
                            %msub
                              %mi L
                              %mi gf
                          %mrow
                            %mi δ
                            %msup
                              %mi ϕ
                              %mi A
                        %mo )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\mathbf{L}'
                      \\coloneqq
                      \\left(
                      \-\mathbf{L}
                      +
                      \\mathbf{L}_{BRST}
                      \\right)
                      \\left( \phi', (\phi')^\ddagger_A  = -\frac{\overset{\leftarrow}{\delta}_{EL} L_{gf}}{\delta \phi^A}  \right)
                      \\,.
              %p
                In this form BV-gauge fixing is considered traditionally (e.g.
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a{:href => "gauge+fixing#Henneaux90"} Hennaux 90, section 8.3, page 83, equation (76b) and item (iii)
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
            %p#AdjoiningAuiliaryFields
              %strong
                adjoining
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contractible+chain+complexes"} contractible cochain complexes
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/auxiliary+fields"} auxiliary fields
            %p
              Typically a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+field+theory"} Lagrangian field theory
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo ,
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi L
