                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gaussian-averaged+Lorenz+gauge"} Gaussian-averaged Lorenz gauge
                is
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi F
                        %mi photon
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mrow
                          %mi μ
                          %mi ν
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo =
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msub
                        %mi η
                        %mrow
                          %mi μ
                          %mi ν
                      %msub
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ,
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      (\Delta^{photon}_F)_{\mu \nu}(x,y)
                      \\;=\;
                      \\eta_{\mu \nu} \Delta_F(x,y)
                      \\,,
              %p
                where on the right
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_F(x,y)
                is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Feynman+propagator"} Feynman propagator
                of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+field+theory"} free
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mass"} massless
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+scalar+field"} real scalar field
                (def.
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FeynmanPropagatorForKleinGordonEquationOnMinkowskiSpacetime"}
              %p
                This is also called the
                = succeed "." do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/photon+propagator"} photon propagator
              %p
                Hence by prop.
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FeynmanPropagatorAsACauchyPrincipalvalue"}
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fourier+transform+of+distributions"} distributional Fourier transform
                of the photon propagator is
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mover
                          %mrow
                            %msubsup
                              %mi Δ
                              %mi F
                              %mi photon
                          %mo ^
                        %mrow
                          %mi μ
                          %mi ν
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo =
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mfrac
                        %mn 1
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %msup
                            %mi k
                            %mi μ
                          %msub
                            %mi k
                            %mi μ
                          %mo +
                          %mi i
                          %msup
                            %mn 0
                            %mo +
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\widehat{\Delta^{photon}_F}_{\mu \nu}(k)
                      \\;=\;
                      \\frac{1}{- k^\mu k_\mu + i 0^+}
                      \\,.
            %p
              (this is a special case of
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "gauge+fixing#Khavkine14"} Khavkine 14 (99)
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "perturbative+algebraic+quantum+field+theory#Rejzner16"} Rejzner 16, (7.20)
            .proof
              %h6#proof_3 Proof
              %p
                The Gaussian-averaged Lorenz gauge-fixed equations of motion
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:LorenzGaugeFixedEOMForVacuumElectromagnetism"} (205)
                of the electromagnetic field are just
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi p
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (p+1)
                uncoupled
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mass"} massless
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Klein-Gordon+equations"} Klein-Gordon equations
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wave+equations"} wave equations
                (example
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EquationOfMotionOfFreeRealScalarField"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi p
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (p+1)
                real components of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electromagnetic+field"} electromagnetic field
                (“
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+potential"}> vector potential
                ”)
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo □
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mi μ
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                      %mphantom
                        %mi AAAA
                      %mi μ
                      %mo ∈
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ⋯
                      %mo ,
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\Box A_\mu = 0\phantom{AAAA} \mu \in \{0,1,\cdots, p\}
                      \\,.
              %p
                This shows that the propoagator is proportional to that of the
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+scalar+field"} real scalar field
              %p
                To see that the index structure is as claimed, recall that the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/domain"} domain
                and
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codomain"} codomain
                of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/advanced+and+retarded+propagators"} advanced and retarded propagators
                in def.
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AdvancedAndRetardedGreenFunctions"}
                is
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi Γ
                                %mi Σ
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi T
                              %mi Σ
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                              %mover
                                %mo ⟶
                                %mrow
                                  %mo (
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %msub
                                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} G
                                    %mo ±
                                  %msub
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                    %mrow
                                      %mi μ
                                      %mi ν
                                  %mo )
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi Γ
                                %mi Σ
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msup
                                %mi T
                                %mo *
                              %mi Σ
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{
                      \\Gamma_\Sigma(T\Sigma)
                      \&amp;\overset{\left( (\mathrm{G}_{\pm})_{\mu \nu} \right)}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                      \\Gamma_\Sigma(T^\ast \Sigma)
                      }
              %p
                corresponding to a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+operator"} differential operator
                for the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equations+of+motion"} equations of motion
                which by
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:ElectromagneticFieldEulerLagrangeForm"} (64)
                and
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:LorenzGaugeFixedEOMForVacuumElectromagnetism"} (205)
                is given by
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi Γ
                                %mi Σ
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msup
                                %mi T
                                %mo *
                              %mi Σ
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                              %mover
                                %mo ⟶
                                %mrow
                                  %msup
                                    %mi η
                                    %mrow
                                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                      %mn 1
                                  %mo ∘
                                  %mo □
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi Γ
                                %mi Σ
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi T
                              %mi Σ
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi A
                                %mi μ
                            %mtd
                              %mo ↦
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mi η
                                %mrow
                                  %mi μ
                                  %mi ν
                              %mo □
                              %msub
                                %mi A
                                %mi ν
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{
                      \\Gamma_\Sigma(T^\ast \Sigma)
                      \&amp;\overset{ \eta^{-1} \circ \Box }{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                      \\Gamma_\Sigma(T \Sigma)
                      \\\
                      A_\mu &amp;\mapsto&amp; \eta^{\mu \nu} \Box A_\nu
                      }
              %p
                Then the defining equation
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:AdvancedRetardedGreenFunctionIsRightInverseToDiffOperator"} (93)
                for the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/advanced+and+retarded+Green+functions"} advanced and retarded Green functions
                is, in terms of their
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integral+kernels"} integral kernels
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/advanced+and+retarded+propagators"} advanced and retarded propagators
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Δ
                        %mo ±
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_{\pm}
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi η
                        %mrow
                          %mi μ
                          %mo ′
                          %mi μ
                      %mo □
                      %munder
                        %mo ∫
                        %mrow
                          %mi y
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi Δ
                        %mo ±
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mrow
                          %mi μ
                          %mi ν
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %msup
                        %mi A
                        %mi ν
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %msub
                        %mi dvol
                        %mi Σ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %msup
                        %mi A
                        %mi ν
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\eta^{\mu' \mu} \Box \underset{y \in X}{\int} (\Delta_{\pm})_{\mu \nu}((-),y) A^{\nu}(y) \, dvol_\Sigma(x)
                      \=
                      A^\nu(x)
                      \\,.
              %p This shows that
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi Δ
                        %mo ±
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mrow
                          %mi μ
                          %mi ν
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo =
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msub
                        %mi η
                        %mrow
                          %mi μ
                          %mi ν
                      %msub
                        %mi Δ
                        %mo ±
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      (\Delta_{\pm})_{\mu \nu}
                      \\;=\;
                      \\eta_{\mu\nu} \Delta_{\pm}
              %p
                with
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Δ
                        %mo ±
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_{\pm}
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/advanced+and+retarded+propagator"} advanced and retarded propagator
                of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+field+theory"} free
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+scalar+field"} real scalar field
                on
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
                (prop.
                = succeed ")," do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AdvancedRetardedPropagatorsForKleinGordonOnMinkowskiSpacetime"}
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi Δ
                                %mrow
                                  %mi μ
                                  %mi ν
                            %mtd
                              %mo =
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msub
                                %mi Δ
                                %mo +
                              %msub
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mrow
                                  %mi μ
                                  %mi ν
                              %mo −
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msub
                                %mi Δ
                                %mo −
                              %msub
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mrow
                                  %mi μ
                                  %mi ν
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo =
                              %msub
                                %mi η
                                %mrow
                                  %mi μ
                                  %mi ν
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msub
                                %mi Δ
                                %mo +
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %msub
                                %mi Δ
                                %mo −
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo =
                              %msub
                                %mi η
                                %mrow
                                  %mi μ
                                  %mi ν
                              %mi Δ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\begin{aligned}
                      \\Delta_{\mu \nu}
                      \&amp;=
                      (\Delta_+)_{\mu \nu}
                      \-
                      (\Delta_-)_{\mu \nu}
                      \\\
                      \&amp; =
                      \\eta_{\mu \nu} (\Delta_+ - \Delta_-)
                      \\\
                      \&amp; =
                      \\eta_{\mu \nu} \Delta
                      \\end{aligned}
            %p Next we compute the gauge-invariant on-shell polynomial observables of the electromagnetic field. The result will involve the following concept:
            #LinearObservablesOfElectromagenticFieldWavePolarization.num_defn
              %h6#definition_3 Definition
              %p
                %strong
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wave+polarization"} wave polarization
                  of linear
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/observables"} observables
                  of the
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electromagnetic+field"} electromagnetic field
              %p
                Consider the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electromagnetic+field"} electromagnetic field
                on
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Σ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+bundle"} field bundle
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cotangent+bundle"} cotangent bundle
              %p The space of off-shell linear observables is spanned by the point evaluation observables
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi e
                        %mi μ
                      %msub
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi A
                        %mi μ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ∈
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi LinObs
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi T
                        %mo *
                      %mi Σ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      e^\mu \mathbf{A}_\mu(x)
                      \\;\in\;
                      LinObs(T^\ast \Sigma)
              %p where
              %ol
                %li
                  %p
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi e
                          %mo =
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msup
                            %mi e
                            %mi μ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ∈
                          %msup
                            %mi ℝ
                            %mrow
                              %mi p
                              %mo ,
                              %mn 1
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e = (e^\mu) \in \mathbb{R}^{p,1}
                    is some vector;
                %li
                  %p
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi x
                          %mo ∈
                          %msup
                            %mi ℝ
                            %mrow
                              %mi p
                              %mo ,
                              %mn 1
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in \mathbb{R}^{p,1}
                    is some point in Minkowski spacetime
                %li
                  %p
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi A
                            %mi μ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mi A
                          %mo ↦
                          %msub
                            %mi A
                            %mi μ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{A}_\mu(x) \;\colon\; A \mapsto A_\mu(x)
                  %p
                    is the functional which sends a section
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi A
                          %mo ∈
                          %msub
                            %mi Γ
                            %mi Σ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi E
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo =
                          %msup
                            %mi Ω
                            %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi Σ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in \Gamma_\Sigma(E) = \Omega^1(\Sigma)
                    to its
                    = succeed "-component" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi μ
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu
                    = succeed "." do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi x
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              %p
                After
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fourier+transform+of+distributions"} Fourier transform of distributions
                this is
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi e
                        %mi μ
                      %msub
                        %mover
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi A
                          %mo ^
                        %mi μ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ∈
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi LinObs
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi T
                        %mo *
                      %mi Σ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      e^\mu \widehat{\mathbf{A}}_\mu(k)
                      \\;\in\;
                      LinObs(T^\ast \Sigma)
              %p
                for
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi k
                        %mi μ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∈
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mi p
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k = (k_\mu) \in (\mathbb{R}^{p,1})^\ast
                the
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wave+vector"} wave vector
