            %p#FreeQuantumBVDifferential
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BV-operator"} free quantum BV-differential
            %p
              So far we have discussed the plain (graded-commutative)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+of+quantum+observables"} algebra of quantum observables
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+fixing"} gauged fixed
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+field+theory"} free
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+field+theory"} Lagrangian field theory
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/deformation+quantization"} deforming
              the commutative pointwise product of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/observables"} observables
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+fixing"} gauge fixing
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential"} differential
              making it a
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+graded-commutative+superalgebra"} differential graded-commutative superalgebra
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BV-differential"} BV-differential
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
