                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_{int} \in LocObs(E_{\text{BV-BRST}})[ [\hbar, g, j] ]
                by definition has compact spacetime support, the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scattering+amplitudes"} scattering amplitudes
                in remark
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FromAxiomaticSMatrixScatteringAmplitudes"}
                describe
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scattering"} scattering
                processes for
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interactions"} interactions
                that vanish (are “
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adiabatic+switching"}> adiabatically switched off
                ”) outside a compact subset of
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/causal+perturbation+theory"} causal perturbation theory
                to work.
              %p There are several aspects to this:
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    (
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adiabatic+limit"}> adiabatic limit
                    ) On the one hand, real physical interactions
