              %p
                If instead of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unshuffles"} unshuffles
                (i.e.
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partitions"} partitions
                into non-empty subsequences preserving the original order) we took partitions into arbitrarily ordered subsequences, we would be overcounting by the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/factorial"} factorial
                of the length of the subsequences, and hence the above may be equivalently written as:
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
