            %p
              In (
              %a{:href => "S-matrix#EpsteinGlaser73"}> Epstein-Glaser 73
              ) this is phrased in terms of splitting of distributions. In (
              %a{:href => "perturbative+algebraic+quantum+field+theory#BrunettiFredenhagen00"}> Brunetti-Fredenhagen 00, sections 4 and 7
              ) the perspective via
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extension+of+distributions"} extension of distributions
              is introduced, following (
              %a{:href => "perturbative+algebraic+quantum+field+theory#Stora93"}> Stora 93
              ). Review is in (
              %a{:href => "perturbative+algebraic+quantum+field+theory#Duetsch18"}> Dütsch 18, section 3.3.2
              ).
            %p
              Proposition
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TimeOrderedProductAwayFromDiagonal"}
              already shows that the freedom in choosing the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/renormalization"} ("re"-)normalization
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/time-ordered+products"} time-ordered products
              is at most that of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extensions+of+distributions"} extending
              them to the “
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fat+diagonal"}> fat diagonal
              ”, where at least one pair of interaction points coincides. The following proposition
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RenormalizationIsInductivelyExtensionToDiagonal"}
              says that when making these choices
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/induction"} inductively
              in the arity of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/time-ordered+products"} time-ordered products
              as in def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ExtensionOfTimeOrderedProoductsRenormalization"}
              then the available choice of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/renormalization"} ("re"-)normalization)
              at each stage is in fact only that of extension to the actual
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagonal"} diagonal
              %em all
              interaction points coincide:
            #RenormalizationIsInductivelyExtensionToDiagonal.num_prop
