              %p
                By the assumption that the
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi T
                        %mi k
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mrow
                          %mi k
                          %mo ≠
                          %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{T_k\}_{k \neq n}
                satisfy causal factorization, this implies that the corresponding time-ordered products commute:
              #eq:TimeOrderedProductsOfMixedIntersectionsCommute.maruku-equation
                %span.maruku-eq-number (241)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi I
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ∩
                      %mover
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi I
                            %mn 2
                        %mo ¯
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mover
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi I
                            %mn 1
                        %mo ¯
                      %mo ∩
                      %msub
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi I
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo =
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mover
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi I
                            %mn 1
                        %mo ¯
                      %mo ∩
                      %msub
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi I
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi I
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ∩
                      %mover
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi I
                            %mn 2
                        %mo ¯
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      T(\mathbf{I}_1 \cap \overline{\mathbf{I}_2})
                      \\,
                      T(\overline{\mathbf{I}_1} \cap \mathbf{I}_2)
                      \\;=\;
                      T(\overline{\mathbf{I}_1} \cap \mathbf{I}_2)
                      \\,
                      T(\mathbf{I}_1 \cap \overline{\mathbf{I}_2})
                      \\,.
              %p
                Using this we find that the identifications of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi T
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo +
                          %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_{n+1}
                on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi I
                            %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}_{I_1}
                and on
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝒞
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi I
                              %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}_{I_2}
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:InductiveIdentificationOfTimeOrderedProductAwayFromDiagonal"} (260)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi X
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi I
                            %mn 1
                      %mo ∩
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi I
                            %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{X}  \in \mathcal{C}_{I_1} \cap \mathcal{C}_{I_2}
                we have
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi T
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msub
                                %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                  %mi I
                                %mn 1
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mi T
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mover
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                      %mi I
                                    %mn 1
                                %mo ¯
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                              %mo =
                              %mi T
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msub
                                %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                  %mi I
                                %mn 1
                              %mo ∩
                              %msub
                                %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                  %mi I
                                %mn 2
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mi T
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msub
                                %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                  %mi I
                                %mn 1
                              %mo ∩
                              %mover
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                      %mi I
                                    %mn 2
                                %mo ¯
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %mi T
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mover
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                      %mi I
                                    %mn 1
                                %mo ¯
                              %mo ∩
                              %msub
                                %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                  %mi I
                                %mn 2
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mi T
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mover
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                      %mi I
                                    %mn 1
                                %mo ¯
                              %mo ∩
                              %mover
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                      %mi I
                                    %mn 2
                                %mo ¯
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo =
                              %mi T
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msub
                                %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                  %mi I
                                %mn 1
                              %mo ∩
                              %msub
                                %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                  %mi I
                                %mn 2
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %munder
                                %mrow
                                  %mi T
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mover
                                    %mrow
                                      %msub
                                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                          %mi I
                                        %mn 1
                                    %mo ¯
                                  %mo ∩
                                  %msub
                                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                      %mi I
                                    %mn 2
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                  %mi T
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %msub
                                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                      %mi I
                                    %mn 1
                                  %mo ∩
                                  %mover
                                    %mrow
                                      %msub
                                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                          %mi I
                                        %mn 2
                                    %mo ¯
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo ⏟
                              %mi T
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mover
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                      %mi I
                                    %mn 1
                                %mo ¯
                              %mo ∩
                              %mover
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                      %mi I
                                    %mn 2
                                %mo ¯
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo =
                              %mi T
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msub
                                %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                  %mi I
                                %mn 2
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mi T
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mover
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                      %mi I
                                    %mn 2
                                %mo ¯
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\begin{aligned}
                      T( \mathbf{I}_1 ) T( \overline{\mathbf{I}_1} )
                      \&amp; =
                      T( \mathbf{I}_1 \cap \mathbf{I}_2 )
                      T( \mathbf{I}_1 \cap \overline{\mathbf{I}_2} )
                      \\,
                      T( \overline{\mathbf{I}_1} \cap \mathbf{I}_2 )
                      T( \overline{\mathbf{I}_1} \cap \overline{\mathbf{I}_2} )
                      \\\
                      \&amp; =
                      T( \mathbf{I}_1 \cap \mathbf{I}_2 )
                      \\underbrace{
                      T( \overline{\mathbf{I}_1} \cap \mathbf{I}_2 )
                      T( \mathbf{I}_1 \cap \overline{\mathbf{I}_2} )
                      }
                      T( \overline{\mathbf{I}_1} \cap \overline{\mathbf{I}_2} )
                      \\\
                      \&amp; =
                      T( \mathbf{I}_2 )
                      T( \overline{\mathbf{I}_2} )
                      \\end{aligned}
              %p
                Here in the first step we expanded out the two factors using
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:InductiveIdentificationOfTimeOrderedProductAwayFromDiagonal"} (260)
                for
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi I
                          %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I_2
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:TimeOrderedProductsOfMixedIntersectionsCommute"} (261)
                and in the last step we used again
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:InductiveIdentificationOfTimeOrderedProductAwayFromDiagonal"} (260)
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi I
                          %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I_1
              %p To conclude, let
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mrow
                          %mo (
                          %msub
                            %mi χ
                            %mi I
                          %mo ∈
                          %msubsup
                            %mi C
                            %mi cp
                            %mn ∞
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msup
                            %mi Σ
                            %mrow
                              %mi n
                              %mo +
                              %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo )
                        %mfrac{:linethickness => "0"}
                          %mrow
                            %mrow
                              %mi I
                              %mo ⊂
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                              %mn 1
                              %mo ,
                              %mi ⋯
                              %mo ,
                              %mi n
                              %mo +
                              %mn 1
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %mrow
                            %mrow
                              %mi I
                              %mo ,
                              %mover
                                %mi I
                                %mo ¯
                              %mo ≠
                              %mi ∅
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\left(
                      \\chi_I
                      \\in
                      C^\infty_{cp}(\Sigma^{n+1})
                      \\right)_{ { I \subset \{1, \cdots, n+1\} } \atop { I, \overline{I} \neq \emptyset } }
              %p
                be a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partition+of+unity"} partition of unity
                subordinate to the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+cover"} open cover
                formed by the
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝒞
                          %mi I
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}_I
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi X
                      %mo ∈
                      %msup
                        %mi Σ
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo +
                          %mn 1
                      %mo ∖
                      %mi diag
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Σ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{X} \in \Sigma^{n+1} \setminus diag(\Sigma)
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi T
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo +
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ≔
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                        %mfrac{:linethickness => "0"}
                          %mrow
                            %mrow
                              %mi I
                              %mo ∈
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                              %mn 1
                              %mo ,
                              %mi ⋯
                              %mo ,
                              %mi n
                              %mo +
                              %mn 1
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %mrow
                            %mrow
                              %mi I
                              %mo ,
                              %mover
                                %mi I
                                %mo ¯
                              %mo ≠
                              %mi ∅
                      %msub
                        %mi χ
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi I
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mover
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi I
                        %mo ¯
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      T_{n+1}(\mathbf{X})
                      \\;\coloneqq\;
                      \\underset{
                      { I \in \{1, \cdots, n+1\} }
                      \\atop
                      { I, \overline{I} \neq \emptyset }
                      }{\sum}
                      \\chi_i(\mathbf{X}) T( \mathbf{I} ) T( \overline{\mathbf{I}} )
              %p is well defined and satisfies causal factorization.
            %p
              Since
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/renormalization"} ("re"-)normalization
              involves making choices, there is the freedom to impose further conditions that one may want to have satisfied. These are called
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/renormalization+conditions"} renormalization conditions
            #RenormalizationConditions.num_defn
              %h6#definition_17 Definition
              %p
                %strong
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/renormalization+conditions"}> renormalization conditions
                  ,
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/protection+from+quantum+corrections"} protection from quantum corrections
                  and
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+anomalies"} quantum anomalies
              %p
                Let
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi E
                        %mtext BV-BRST
                      %mo ,
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi L
                      %mo ′
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi H
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (E_{\text{BV-BRST}}, \mathbf{L}', \Delta_H )
                be a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relativistic+field+theory"} relativistic
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+field+theory"} free
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vacuum"} vacuum
                according to def.
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#VacuumFree"}
              %p
                Then a condition
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
                on
                = succeed "-ary" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi T
                        %mi k
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msup
                        %mrow
                          %mo (
                          %mfrac{:linethickness => "0"}
                            %mrow
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mrow
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mi LocObs
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi E
                            %mtext BV-BRST
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi ℏ
                          %mo ,
                          %mi g
                          %mo ,
                          %mi j
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mfrac{:linethickness => "0"}
                            %mrow
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mrow
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mo )
                        %mrow
                          %msubsup
                            %mo ⊗
                            %mrow
                              %mi ℂ
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                              %mi ℏ
                              %mo ,
                              %mi g
                              %mo ,
                              %mi j
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mi k
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi PolyObs
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi E
                        %mtext BV-BRST
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi reg
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℏ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi g
                      %mo ,
                      %mi j
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      T_k
                      \\;\colon\;
                      \\left(
                      {\, \atop \,}
                      LocObs(E_{\text{BV-BRST}})[ [\hbar, g, j] ]
                      {\, \atop \,}
                      \\right)^{\otimes^k_{\mathbb{C}[ [\hbar, g, j] ]}}
                      \\longrightarrow
                      PolyObs(E_{\text{BV-BRST}})_{reg}((\hbar))[ [g , j] ]
              %p
                is called a
                %em renormalization condition
                if
              %ol
                %li
                  %p
                    it holds for the unique
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/time-ordered+products"} time-ordered products
                    away from coinciding spacetime arguments (according to prop.
                    = succeed ");" do
                      %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TimeOrderedProductAwayFromDiagonal"}
                %li
                  %p
                    whenever it holds for all unrestricted
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi T
                            %mrow
                              %mi k
                              %mo ≤
                              %mi n
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_{k \leq n}
                    for some
                    = succeed "," do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi ℕ
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi T
                            %mrow
                              %mi n
                              %mo +
                              %mn 1
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_{n+1}
                    restricted away from the diagonal:
                  .maruku-equation
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi P
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi T
                            %mi k
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mrow
                              %mi k
                              %mo ≤
                              %mi n
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mo ⇒
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mi P
                          %mrow
                            %mo (
                            %msub
                              %mi T
                              %mrow
                                %mi n
                                %mo +
                                %mn 1
                            %msub
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                              %mrow
                                %msup
                                  %mi Σ
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi n
                                    %mo +
                                    %mn 1
                                %mo ∖
                                %mi diag
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi Σ
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo )
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mo .
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                          P(T_k)_{k \leq n}
                          \\;\Rightarrow\;
                          P\left(
                          T_{n+1}\vert_{\Sigma^{n+1} \setminus diag(\Sigma)}
                          \\right)
                          \\,.
              %p
                This means that a renormalization condition is a condition that may consistently be imposed degreewise in an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/induction"} inductive
                construction of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/time-ordered+products"} time-ordered products
                by degreewise
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extension+of+distributions"} extension
                to the
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagonal"} diagonal
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RenormalizationIsInductivelyExtensionToDiagonal"}
              %p
                If specified renormalization conditions
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi P
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{P_i\}
                completely remove any freedom in the choice of time-ordered products for a given
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+observable"} quantum observable
                = succeed "." do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/protection+from+quantum+corrections"} protects the observable against quantum corrections
              %p
                If for specified renormalization conditions
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
